snippet.textDisplay:
@pickwick3970Because corporations, if they had the ability to do so and in a cost effective manner, would try to replace most, if not all of their employees with AI. You can already see it with AI “art” being used in advertising. In my personal opinion, AI should be used to assist, but never replace; and in the scenario that it should replace, then there should be adequate support for those whose jobs are made irrelevant.

It’s less a fear of technological advancement, but more a fear of what said advancements will be used for and who it’s being used by.

Edit: I realized you used the word “Barbaric” to make yourself sound smarter.

